  "id": "pupillary-reflex",
  "term": "pupillary reflex",
  "definition": "In this historical source, the pupillary reflex means the pupil’s automatic change in size in response to stimulation. Normal reactions described are narrowing to light, widening with sensory stimulation, and narrowing along with accommodation and convergence for near vision.",
